{"kind":"assert","text":"CUT-A ruling on c54a127d. The list is accepted, with the fifth\ndocument, `docs/security/trust-boundaries.md`. The script proposal\nis accepted: one name map, one tracked file, a check with the\nproduction parsers before the write, and no write on a failure.\n\nThe historical boundary is confirmed. The records under\n`notes/implementation` keep their old identifiers, and so do the\nsigned packets. No active test, example or current document keeps a\nhosted scope ID.\n\nDecision 1. Head A is demo, grow and lending. The script refuses\n`artroom-scope`, `sandbox`, and each name that is not in the map.\nartroom-scope gets no register in this cutover, and Hugh decides\nwhether the Worker is deleted. Commons and Connect keep their\nplaceholders.\n\nDecision 2, the installed list. The default appends the new root\none time and keeps the others, under the bound of 32. One flag,\n`--only`, writes the list as the new root alone. Head A uses\n`--only`, because main reads no room of a retired root.\n\nDecision 2, the offer. Head A turns Browser Start on for dap-demo.\nThe bootstrap arguments `--start-origin`, `--deployment` and\n`--definition` are accepted. The script infers no value. It refuses\nwhen the file holds a `DEPLOYMENT` that differs from the argument.\nHead A also tracks `DEPLOYMENT` in the demo file, so that the file\nalone shows that the offer and the Worker agree. I give the live\nvalue in the END act of the window, read from the deployed version.\n\nOne more check in the script test: the output for one name changes\nno byte of another tracked file.\n\nStart the source. Gate order stays: after CDF-1, ahead of the\nclient chain.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}